<p>NASA released the first downlinked images from the Artemis II crew about 1½ days into the mission, showing Earth through and beyond the Orion capsule windows as the four astronauts traveled farther from home on the first crewed moon mission in more than 50 years. By Friday, NASA and multiple outlets said the spacecraft had passed the halfway point between Earth and the moon, a visible milestone in a mission designed to send astronauts on a lunar flyby before returning to Earth. The images and crew remarks helped turn the trip into a shared global moment. Commander Reid Wiseman photographed first a curved slice of Earth and later the full globe, while the astronauts described seeing the planet and the northern lights from deep space. The updates highlighted both the technical progress of the Artemis program and a more personal truth: after decades without astronauts heading moonward, people are once again watching Earth shrink into the distance from a crewed spacecraft.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8KarrZZhfud4PmMGzO9GposzTNku7pXnbzzvYLTuyac2hV42_HNeEB182_C6_wdgYvwCXZ7wAEHK_EkjF4nGFJQvmI7TgfcCZppgoPtWtkzE2I1CnzSLXstmkXgPMcxai2i1bLR6C7zxHG0bnXJkZbDslo1dNDslZ7B_7c6j2nj5WS7s-LJpI5ao13My5o6oiNS3gypL-Y_8J7zDikTpD_v913Q_O62RZOdhaRQJ1GcnDtHLJ5FNFoClfoJ0h5vBTQ-IStKuT6oYxwWA6s1p' alt='Image released as Artemis II astronauts shared a view of Earth while passing halfway to the moon' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Distance marker: Al Jazeera reported that the crew was about 100,000 miles, or 160,000km, from Earth as they continued closing in on the moon.</li><li>First commander shot: Commander Reid Wiseman took the first released photo, showing a curved slice of Earth framed in one of Orion&#x27;s windows.</li><li>Crew contact: The astronauts made video contact with Earth on Thursday and described the views from deep space as breathtaking.</li><li>Aurora view: The Guardian said the crew saw the entire Earth along with the northern lights, a sight the astronauts called &#x27;the most spectacular moment&#x27;.</li></ul><blockquote>The most spectacular moment - Artemis II astronauts</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>NASA: NASA marked the mission milestone by posting that the crew was halfway to the moon, underscoring the progress of the lunar flyby journey. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/apr/03/artemis-ii-astronauts-rocket-towards-the-moon-after-breaking-free-of-earths-orbit'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Reid Wiseman: Wiseman documented the journey by taking the first released Orion photo of Earth, giving the public a crew-eye view from deep space. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce8jzr423p9o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Artemis II crew: During a video link with Earth, the crew described the sights from deep space as extraordinary, drawing attention to the experience of seeing Earth from afar. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/watch-artemis-ii-crew-make-contact-with-earth-describe-breathtaking-sights/article70820885.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nasa-artemis-ii-astronauts-capture-earths-brilliant-blue-beauty-from-orion-spacecraft-ahead-of-moon-visit-11309249#publisher=newsstand'>Artemis II&#x27;s Moonbound Astronauts Capture Earth&#x27;s Brilliant Blue Beauty</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/apr/03/artemis-ii-astronauts-rocket-towards-the-moon-after-breaking-free-of-earths-orbit'>Artemis II astronauts share image of Earth as they pass halfway to the moon</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3349005/artemis-iis-moon-bound-astronauts-share-first-images-earths-brilliant-blue-beauty'>Artemis II’s moon-bound astronauts share first images of Earth’s brilliant blue beauty</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/artemis-astronauts-pass-half-way-point-on-way-to-moon'>Artemis astronauts more than halfway to Moon, putting Earth in rearview</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/watch-artemis-ii-crew-make-contact-with-earth-describe-breathtaking-sights/article70820885.ece'>Watch: Artemis II crew make contact with Earth, describe breathtaking sights</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce8jzr423p9o'>Artemis II crew now halfway to Moon as they take &#x27;spectacular&#x27; image of Earth</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/4/nasa-unveils-first-images-of-earth-from-artemis-ii'>NASA unveils first images of Earth from Artemis II</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>